  "id": "COMPOUND:11458 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Flumedroxone is implicated in the regulation of Neuropilin-2 through a multi-step pathway involving dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including (2''s,3''s)-Epoxyangeloyldecursinol and 5,7-dimethoxy-8-[(E)-3-oxobut-1-enyl]chromen-2-one, which in turn target Neuropilin-2. The evidence suggests that Flumedroxone may act through a common intermediate, dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is a target of several compounds that ultimately interact with Neuropilin-2. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Flumedroxone influences Neuropilin-2, possibly through the modulation of metabolic pathways that are shared among the compounds involved. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Flumedroxone and Neuropilin-2, with the dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 acting as a central mediator in this interaction.",
